# Trivy findings deliberately accepted for a limited time. Each line expires on its
# exp: date, after which the image check fails again until it is fixed or re-reviewed.
# Approved by Attila Madarasz, 12 Oct 2026 (SCRUM-38).
# Extended from 26 Oct to 2 Nov 2026 (SCRUM-60) because no Caddy image built with Go >= 1.26.10
# was out yet; approved by Attila Madarasz by merging that change.
#
# Base image caddy:2-alpine: Caddy's binary is built with Go 1.26.8 and
# golang.org/x/net v0.59.0. The Go security release of 11 Oct 2026 fixes these in
# Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 and x/net 0.60.0; no Caddy release is built with them yet.
# Exposure is low until launch: staging is reached only on the LAN and the tailnet,
# and the site's Caddy sits behind the staging gateway on plain HTTP/1.1.
# Remove this block once a Caddy release built with Go >= 1.26.10 is out (rebuild,
# and the scan should pass without it). A weekly workflow, caddy-base-check.yml,
# scans the base image without this file and says when that has happened (SCRUM-60).

# HTTP/2 (x/net and stdlib): GO-2026-6603, 6610, 6611, 6612, 6617
